WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.640
At the 100th Anniversary

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.810
of the Chinese Communist Party in 2021,

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.820
Chinese President Xi
Jinping outlined his vision

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.750
for the Chinese Dream.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.440
We will achieve the goal of building

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.950
a great modern socialist
country in all respects

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.690
and fulfill the Chinese Dream

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.483
of national rejuvenation.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.930
The fact that China and Xi Jinping

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.820
talk about a China Dream

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.510
really reminds us that great powers

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.660
need to have grand narratives

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.927
in the same way that the United States

00:00:38.927 --> 00:00:41.513
and the narrative about
the American Dream.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.470
To make that China Dream a reality

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.543
and achieve the great rejuvenation,

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.060
Chinese leaders believe they must have

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.420
the world's most powerful military.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:00:59.810
A strong country

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:01.508
must have a strong military,

00:01:01.508 --> 00:01:04.320
as only then can it guarantee

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.110
the security of the nation.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.580
The Party came to recognize
the irrefutable truth

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.887
that it must build a
people's military of its own.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:20.850
China's military power

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.330
has been growing at an incredible speed

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.250
over the last 20 years.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.430
In terms of fear and influence,

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:29.710
we absolutely know that China
wants to be dominant in Asia.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:31.920
So there is a target to get to that point,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.710
to be a military that is a peer

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:38.770
to the greatest militaries
in the world by 2035.

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:41.650
The competition for
influence is a global one.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.680
And through a multi-decade trajectory

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.620
filled by planning, money, and pragmatism,

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.760
China's building a military that allows it

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.570
to shape the 21st century,

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.904
just as the US shape the 20th.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.300
The most interesting question

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.960
when it comes to China's growth

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.820
and what spurred the growth is actually,

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.220
you don't have to look back

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.420
50 years, 40 years, 30 years.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.410
Actually, most of these
changes have happened

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.840
in the past 25 years.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.800
So if you go 25 years ago,

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.490
the Chinese economy was
smaller than France's economy.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:33.160
They took up 3% of global GDP.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:35.850
They had a military that you could hardly

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:37.170
even call it a military, right?

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.580
A Navy that couldn't
sail beyond the coast.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:43.850
Until second half of 1990s,

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.330
the Chinese defense budget

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.470
was absolutely negligible. at some point

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.003
less than $15 billion,

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.903
2.5 million troops.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:00.320
But now, China is either
the second or third

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.723
most powerful military in the world.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.960
And it's got there largely as always

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:08.560
through spending a lot of money.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.120
Thanks to a 740% increase
in military spending

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.520
as well as elite focus,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.430
they've now built one of the
most formidable militaries

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.990
that this world has ever seen.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.770
China's defense expenditures

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:25.690
have multiplied by 12 times since 2000.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.390
And while America's military budget

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.980
is nearly four times that of China's,

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.410
it does not mean that the US' military

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.160
is four times as powerful.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:36.900
And that's because of
different objectives.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.080
The United States is
trying to project power

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.120
all around the world.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.893
That is extremely costly.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.250
The US spends huge amounts of their money

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.230
on the global war for
terror in the Middle East

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.280
in the past two decades.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.420
And of course, China's lowers

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.820
the defense construction cost

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:58.093
and it has cheaper man power.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.980
That budget of the United States,

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:03.270
it's used for the United States to act

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:05.030
as the global guardian

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.190
of the Labor International Order.

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:10.270
Instead, the smaller budget of China

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:14.040
is mostly concentrated in one region.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.210
We have hundreds of bases overseas.

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:17.470
China has one.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:22.170
So they're really promoting
their military power regionally.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.960
And so that's one way that they can

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.460
out compete the United States.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:32.480
I have been very, very straightforward

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.830
and blunt with President Putin.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.710
We will impose the most severe sanctions

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.760
that have ever been imposed,

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.033
economic sanctions.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.180
When the US is distracted elsewhere,

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.040
whether it's over the Ukraine issue now

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:51.595
or the war on terror for
two decades beforehand,

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.810
the United States cannot
compete with China.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.840
Countries like the US, the UK, Australia,

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.680
European countries
overlook the understanding

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.840
of China's strategic culture.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.310
And we didn't want to accept the fact

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:08.663
that while we were trading with China,

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.683
China was growing militarily.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.740
To understand the magnitude

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:19.000
of China's determination in
achieving its national goals,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.760
look no further than the
Belt and Road Initiative,

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:24.807
china's trillion dollar
global infrastructure plan

00:05:24.807 --> 00:05:27.580
and the centerpiece of
President Xi Jinping's

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:29.010
foreign policy.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.530
The Belt and Road Initiative

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.630
is one of the big Chinese economic plans

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.826
to build power and influence in the world.

00:05:34.826 --> 00:05:36.880
The United States could have
done 10 of those, right?

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.130
But instead we fought
the war in Afghanistan.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.660
And while the US and the EU

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:43.750
are busy policing the world,

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.800
China has focused on
building infrastructure.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.520
And when it comes to the military,

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:50.960
it has had the same laser focus.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.930
The Chinese were actually
extremely pragmatic

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:56.350
in deciding how to go about matching

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:59.160
its military capacities
and increasing them,

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.060
so that it could challenge US dominance.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.720
And they did so basically with weapons

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:06.900
that are much cheaper to produce

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.963
than the things that they destroy.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.490
Of course, there are certain narrow areas

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.370
where Chinese are more advanced.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:23.893
These areas include the
hypersonic missiles.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.760
What we saw was a very significant event

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:32.510
of a test of a hypersonic weapon system,

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:34.200
and it is very concerning.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.780
I think I saw in some of the newspapers

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:39.020
that they used the term Sputnik moment.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:41.180
What they're really,
the US, is really saying

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:43.140
is that these hypersonic missiles

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:45.070
could change the game.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:48.630
China is investing in hypersonic missiles

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:51.260
principally to show the rest of the world

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.110
that it's capable of developing

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:55.810
cutting edge military technologies.

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:56.790
Because of the name,

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:58.670
people focus the hypersonic part

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:00.290
and how fast they go,

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.350
but actually the biggest issue

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:03.570
when it comes to defenses

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:06.430
is that they can fly very low

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:08.470
because of the circular
nature of the Earth.

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:09.990
If you have a radar system,

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:13.030
you don't see it until
close to the last minute,

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:14.920
which makes it difficult to intercept.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.540
The broader strategic issue

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.460
that China is more advanced in this area

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.960
than the United States is

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.300
brings up a lot of anxiety about

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:25.373
how the United States
technologically is falling behind.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:31.110
They shown this on parade in 2019

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:33.740
and the Americans are only expected

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:37.500
to have a first battery of similar missile

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:40.160
for testing in 2023.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.250
So that's incredibly,

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.703
that's an incredible lead.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:51.460
And while the US is trailing China

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.460
in hypersonic technology,

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:55.560
China is quickly closing the gap

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:57.580
when it comes to Naval Forces.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:01.150
In 2015, China published a white paper

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:03.290
on China's military strategy,

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:05.580
where the Chinese elites stated

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.920
that China needs to move beyond

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:11.263
an old fashioned, traditional
mentality-based on land power.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:15.080
The Americans understand that the Chinese

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:18.180
are gradually winning the arms race.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:22.270
They're simply building more
ships than the American can.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:25.350
The Americans have been
losing their manufacturing

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.920
for generations.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:29.760
The best example is ship building.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:32.430
China is the country with the biggest

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:35.980
commercial ship building
industry in the world.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:40.120
China basically builds 40%
of the ships in the world.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:45.120
The US and its European
allies build about 1%.

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.050
It allows the Chinese to produce ships

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:48.690
at an extraordinary rate,

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:52.550
and to overtake or to
match the US very quickly,

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.453
if they wish to.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.910
Once you get into wartime,

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:59.230
those advantages, they really determine

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:01.270
the ability of the US to win

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.663
the first and second
World Wars for the Allies.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.640
Operating day and night

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:09.590
on a 24-hour mass production schedule,

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.990
America giving wings
to the greatest armada

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:14.890
of fighting ships the
world has ever known.

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:17.200
Many analysts nowadays

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.580
believe that China is already capable

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:22.250
of winning a short-term conflict

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:23.943
within the First Island Chain,

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:30.280
which is this line that
goes from the south of Japan

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:32.950
through Taiwan, down to the Philippines

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.233
and the South China Sea.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.950
In addition to a state of the art Navy

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:44.180
as well as their hypersonic missiles,

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.160
China may also have an edge when it comes

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.560
to how wars are fought
in the 21st century.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:52.190
One of the most worrying areas

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:55.700
of Chinese development
has been cyber warfare.

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:56.990
As much as we know,

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.730
the Chinese have the biggest

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:02.280
cyber forces in the world.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.770
It's important to understand

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:07.710
that the Chinese started
to prioritize cyber warfare

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:10.150
and the information warfare in general

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:12.830
very early in 1990s.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:15.900
They understood that the
key of American advantage

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:18.150
was the information advantage.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:23.150
And to win, they needed to
destroy this American advantage.

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:25.368
They've been able to accelerate

00:10:25.368 --> 00:10:27.590
their arms development programs

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:32.480
by gaining intelligence
on US weapons systems.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:35.450
With cyber, nobody's ever quite sure

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:37.310
about what the other side's capability is

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:38.680
until it's been used.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:40.410
And once it's been used, it's gone

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.720
and you have to develop something else

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:44.480
because it can be dealt
with once it's known.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:46.400
Cyber immediately takes you on

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:49.400
to the question of
artificial intelligence.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:52.720
And Vladimir Putin famously said,

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:56.210
whoever wins that competition
will rule the world.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.970
And the ideas that once you develop AI,

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:02.660
they can either assist or
replace weapon systems.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:05.250
And this emphasis on cyber warfare

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:07.020
and artificial intelligence

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.220
tell us how extremely relevant

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:12.790
continues to be the writing of Sun Tzu,

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:15.390
and in particular, "The Art Of War",

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:18.560
where concepts like disruption, deception,

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.260
know your enemy, win without fight,

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:22.597
remain important.

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:30.380
Ultimately, China's powers

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:32.050
wrapped up in how much influence

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:34.313
their military and their economy have.

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:40.770
But one question still remains,

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:44.930
what does China, as well
as Xi Jinping, really want?

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.810
US-China relations is based on

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.070
our understanding of the Taiwan issue.

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:52.520
The United States keeps the seventh fleet

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:55.109
and other military forces in the area

00:11:55.109 --> 00:11:57.023
to preserve the status quo.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.020
Xi Jinping has kind of decided

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:01.590
that he doesn't like this perpetual

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.750
de facto independence of Taiwan

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:07.033
and he wants to start bringing
Taiwan back into the fold.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.380
The way that the Communist Party

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:10.440
originally wanted to do that

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:12.014
was through peace reunification.

00:12:12.014 --> 00:12:14.314
So close economic and cultural ties

00:12:14.314 --> 00:12:15.830
would convince the people of Taiwan

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:18.103
to voluntarily be a part of the PRC.

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:21.800
That is not happening.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:24.660
The last polls is only 6%
of the people of Taiwan said

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:27.230
that they wanted to be a part of the PRC.

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:28.480
And so now in Mainland China

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.177
there's serious discussion about,

00:12:30.177 --> 00:12:32.880
"Well, if we can't do this peacefully,

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:35.830
domestic Chinese law tells us
it's time to do it by force."

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:40.315
The cross trades relation is a kind

00:12:40.315 --> 00:12:44.363
of stable condition under
the unstable situation.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:50.490
Unification is the final
puzzle piece for China.

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:56.710
China is trying to intimidate
Taiwan and the United States

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:59.723
as well as the other
countries in this region.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:02.460
There is a widespread belief

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:05.090
that over the next 20 to 30 years,

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:07.480
China will be so powerful militarily

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:10.993
that they will be able
to grab Taiwan very easy.

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:15.620
This is still a question mark,

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.450
because regardless of the power of China,

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:20.840
regardless of the fact
that there is a huge

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.690
military gap between China and Taiwan,

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.600
it is extremely difficult for China

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:28.860
to put boots on the ground in Taiwan.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:31.030
And this is because of the complex

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:33.680
urban geography of Taiwan.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:36.790
It's because of the few entry points

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:38.573
on the coast of Taiwan.

00:13:39.704 --> 00:13:42.370
Taiwan will be able to mobilize

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:44.403
a great amount of military reserve.

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.513
It will be able to mobilize its population

00:13:50.513 --> 00:13:52.340
against an invasion.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:54.720
And so regardless of the power of China,

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.723
Taiwan might be China's Vietnam.

